---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---
<LegalLayout title="Dispute Process">
  <h2>For Companies</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe your company's scores are inaccurate, misleading, or based on reviews that violate our Community Guidelines, you can submit a formal dispute.
  </p>

  <h3>Grounds for Dispute</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Factual inaccuracy:</strong> The company name, industry, or headquarters city is wrong.</li>
    <li><strong>Guideline violations:</strong> Specific reviews contain content that violates our <a href="/guidelines" class="text-coral hover:text-coral/80 underline">Community Guidelines</a> (names individuals, contains hate speech, etc.).</li>
    <li><strong>Coordinated manipulation:</strong> Evidence of a coordinated campaign to inflate or deflate scores.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What Disputes Cannot Do</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Remove reviews simply because the scores are low or unflattering.</li>
    <li>Identify individual reviewers. We will never reveal reviewer identity.</li>
    <li>Override aggregate scores. If the reviews are genuine, the scores stand.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Process</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Email <strong>disputes@belongary.com</strong> with the company name, specific concern, and any supporting evidence.</li>
    <li>A human moderator reviews the dispute within 10 business days.</li>
    <li>If a review is found to violate guidelines, it is removed and scores are recalculated.</li>
    <li>The disputing party receives a written response regardless of outcome.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>For Reviewers</h2>
  <p>
    If you submitted a review and want to correct or remove it:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>If you provided an email:</strong> Email us from that address at <strong>support@belongary.com</strong> and request correction or removal. We'll verify the email matches and process your request.</li>
    <li><strong>If you did not provide an email:</strong> We cannot verify ownership of anonymous reviews. For this reason, we strongly encourage providing an email during submission — it's the only way to maintain control over your review.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Timeline</h2>
  <p>
    Most disputes are resolved within 10 business days. Complex cases involving coordinated manipulation may take longer. We'll keep you updated on progress.
  </p>

  <h2>Good Faith</h2>
  <p>
    We take every dispute seriously, but we also protect the integrity of honest reviewer voices. The dispute process is not a mechanism for companies to silence criticism. Abuse of the dispute process — frivolous or bad-faith claims designed to suppress legitimate reviews — will be noted and may affect how future disputes from the same party are handled.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
